        {
          "id": "intro",
          "type": "text",
          "content": "A video element plays inline in jdf.js and the desktop reader. This one points at a hosted file with src; the same element can carry the clip inside a .jdfx bundle instead (see examples/video.jdfx).",
          "style": "body",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 16
          },
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "id": "clip",
          "type": "video",
          "poster": "logo-256.png",
          "title": "JDF vs PDF for RAG — the benchmark video (hosted file)",
          "controls": true,
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 44
          },
          "width": 166,
          "height": 93.4,
          "fit": "contain",
          "src": "demos/rag-benchmark.mp4",
          "transcript": {
            "language": "en",
            "source": "srt-import",
            "created": "2026-09-13T12:42:41.961Z",
            "segments": [
              {
                "t0": 0,
                "t1": 3.6,
                "text": "Twenty-four reports. One hundred ninety-two questions. Same pipeline. PDF versus JDF."
              },
              {
                "t0": 3.6,
                "t1": 7.2,
                "text": "Answer inside the first one thousand tokens: JDF ninety-nine percent, PDF converted to JDF ninety-nine percent, best raw PDF eighty-three percent."
              },
              {
                "t0": 7.2,
                "t1": 10.8,
                "text": "Tokens handed to the model per question: seven hundred fifty-three versus twelve hundred twenty-four. Thirty-eight percent less LLM spend."
              },
              {
                "t0": 10.8,
                "t1": 14.4,
                "text": "Edit one paragraph: JDF re-embeds one chunk of one hundred ninety-two. A PDF re-embeds every chunk of every file. Sixteen times cheaper re-indexing."
              },
              {
                "t0": 14.4,
                "t1": 18,
                "text": "Nine hundred forty-one dollars saved per million questions, measured. Ten times the questions, ten times the saving, estimated."
              },
              {
                "t0": 18,
                "t1": 21.6,
                "text": "Only have PDFs? jdf convert. Eighty percent top-one after conversion."
              },
              {
                "t0": 21.6,
                "t1": 25.2,
                "text": "Measured, not claimed. Run python rag_bench.py --verify yourself."
              }
            ]
          },
          "chapters": [
            {
              "t": 0,
              "title": "Setup"
            },
            {
              "t": 3.6,
              "title": "Accuracy"
            },
            {
              "t": 7.2,
              "title": "Tokens"
            },
            {
              "t": 10.8,
              "title": "Re-indexing"
            },
            {
              "t": 14.4,
              "title": "Savings"
            },
            {
              "t": 18,
              "title": "Convert your PDFs"
            },
            {
              "t": 21.6,
              "title": "Verify"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "cap",
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Figure 1 — hosted video via src (relative URL), poster from the site.",
          "style": "cap",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 146
          },
          "width": 166
        },
        {
          "id": "how",
          "type": "text",
          "content": "Authoring: { \"type\": \"video\", \"resource\": \"clip\", \"poster\": \"poster\", \"title\": \"…\" } with the bytes in resources.videos.clip — or { \"type\": \"video\", \"src\": \"https://…/clip.mp4\" } for a hosted file. jdf chunk indexes the title as [video: …].",
          "style": "body",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 156
          },
          "width": 166
        }
      ]
    }
